  "body": "`store` in `src/tide_cache.py` keeps every tide reading for ever. Readings should expire after a retention period, but how long the harbour keeps a reading is a policy call the repository does not state. Expire stale readings once the period is known.\n\n**Delivers:** `store` no longer keeps readings for ever: a reading held longer than the retention period is dropped from `READINGS`. The period itself is the open question in the section below, and this payload names no value for it.\n\n- Each reading gets a stored-at time when `store` takes it, because `store` accepts an opaque reading with no time of its own (`src/tide_cache.py:4`).\n- Expiry runs inside `store`, the module's only entry point (`src/tide_cache.py:4`); nothing in the repository reads `READINGS` (`src/tide_cache.py:1`).\n\n**Test contract:** Failing tests first, against a controlled clock: a reading inside the period survives a later `store`; a reading past the period is gone after a later `store`; a reading exactly at the period is pinned to whichever side the implementation chooses; a newly stored reading is always kept.\n\n**Files:** `src/tide_cache.py` (modified); `tests/test_tide_cache.py` (new; the repository has no test surface yet, so this path is proposed rather than an existing convention).\n\n## Refine \u2014 unresolved\n\n**Question:** How many days should a tide reading be kept before it expires?\n\n**Evidence gathered:** `src/tide_cache.py:4` stores every reading and `src/tide_cache.py:5` only appends, so there is no expiry and no period to inherit. The other source files and `README.md:1` state no retention period. In the vault, `lore search` on retention, expire, expiry, stale, tide, reading, harbour, policy and cache found no decision: `kind:area`, `kind:adr`, `kind:lesson` and `kind:decision` return nothing, and the tide specs [[spec/fixture-tide-expiry-spec]] and [[spec/fixture-tide-reading-spec]] carry no content on it. Other tasks' escalation sections are scoped to those records and settle nothing here.\n\n**Recommended answer:** 30 days, as a conventional default for operational readings. Nothing in the repository or vault supports this value, so it is a suggestion for the operator to confirm or replace, not a derived fact.\n**Answer:** Keep readings for 21 days.\n",
